# Wheel pickers (mandatory)

All wheel-style pickers in the mobile app **must** use the shared components in `@/components/settings`.

## Use these

| Need | Component | Import |
|------|-----------|--------|
| List of options (duration, enum, etc.) | `WheelPicker` | `@/components/settings` |
| Time / date spinner | `IosWheelDateTimePicker` | `@/components/settings` |
| Time range bottom sheet | `TimeRangePickerSheet` | `@/components/settings` |
| Duration bottom sheet | `DurationPickerSheet` | `@/components/settings` |
| Styling tokens | `wheelPickerTheme`, `nativeWheelPickerProps` | `@/lib/wheelPickerTheme` |
| Selection haptic | `triggerWheelSelectionHaptic` | `@/lib/wheelPickerHaptics` |

## Never use directly in feature code

- `@react-native-picker/picker` — only inside `WheelPicker.tsx`
- `@react-native-community/datetimepicker` — only inside `IosWheelDateTimePicker.tsx`
- Custom `ScrollView` wheels on iOS/Android (web fallback lives inside `WheelPicker.tsx` only)

## Why

Native `UIPickerView` / `UIDatePicker` provide momentum scrolling, natural deceleration, and snap-on-settle — matching Apple HIG. Custom ScrollView pickers stop abruptly and caused infinite-update bugs.

## Adding a new wheel picker

1. Build options as `WheelPickerOption<T>[]`
2. Render `<WheelPicker options={...} value={...} onChange={...} />`
3. For times, use `<IosWheelDateTimePicker mode="time" ... />` or `TimeRangePickerSheet`
4. Do not duplicate picker UI in screen files
